{
  "_notes": [
    "Pirates of the Caribbean V6.0 Stern SAM language revisions.",
    "Decoder constants are one-based file offsets; SAM map offsets are adjusted to CPU-addressed NVRAM offsets.",
    "SAM stores the 4 player scores as 4 x 8-byte (64-bit little-endian) fields: stride 8, not 4. The prior stride-4/length-4 layout mis-read players 2-4 (P2 read the zero high-bytes of P1, etc.). Corrected and validated against real 2-/3-/4-player Metallica dumps (mtl_180h)."
  ],
  "_fileformat": 0.8,
  "_metadata": {
    "version": 5,
    "copyright": [
      "Copyright (C) 2026 by Andre Santana <herrmirto@proton.me>"
    ],
    "license": "GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0",
    "platform": "stern-sam",
    "roms": [
      "potc_600af",
      "potc_600ai",
      "potc_600as"
    ]
  },
  "game_state": {
    "player_count": {
      "_notes": [
        "Stern SAM number-of-players-in-game at fixed NVRAM address 0x02110900 (adjacent to game_over 0x02110904 in the SAM game-state header). Identified from three real played dumps: the only byte that reads exactly 2 / 3 / 4 in 2-, 3- and 4-player games (mtl_180h)."
      ],
      "label": "Player Count",
      "start": "0x02110900",
      "encoding": "int",
      "length": 1
    },
    "scores": [
      {
        "label": "Player 1",
        "start": "0x021109E4",
        "encoding": "int",
        "length": 8
      },
      {
        "label": "Player 2",
        "start": "0x021109EC",
        "encoding": "int",
        "length": 8
      },
      {
        "label": "Player 3",
        "start": "0x021109F4",
        "encoding": "int",
        "length": 8
      },
      {
        "label": "Player 4",
        "start": "0x021109FC",
        "encoding": "int",
        "length": 8
      }
    ],
    "game_over": {
      "_notes": [
        "Stern SAM platform-wide game-in-progress flag at fixed NVRAM address 0x02110904, bit 0x40 (set = game over / no game in progress). The address is independent of the per-game live-score layout and was validated by live headless exercise (boot -> play -> game-over) on mtl_180h, trn_174 and xmn_150: bit 0x40 is set in attract/game-over and clear throughout active play (trn_174 0/242 and xmn_150 0/242 play snapshots set)."
      ],
      "label": "Game Over",
      "start": "0x02110904",
      "encoding": "bool",
      "mask": "0x40"
    },
    "credits": {
      "_notes": [
        "Stern SAM platform-wide credits counter at fixed NVRAM address 0x0211100C (redundant copy at 0x02111014). Identified by the stimulus-response harness (identify_game_state.py): the byte rises as coins are inserted and drops by exactly 1 when a game starts - a pricing-agnostic signature. Confirmed on mtl_180h, trn_174, avs_170, xmn_150."
      ],
      "label": "Credits",
      "start": "0x0211100C",
      "encoding": "int",
      "length": 1
    }
  },
